<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Vanilla Cone: Where Dairy Queen History Began (1940)</h2>
    <p>Long before the invention of the Blizzard or flame-grilled Stackburgers, Dairy Queen was built entirely on a single revolutionary idea: soft serve. When founders J.F. McCullough and Sherb Noble opened the world's very first Dairy Queen in Joliet, Illinois on June 22, 1940, the hand-pulled Vanilla Soft Serve Cone was the entire menu. Over eight decades later, it remains the purest expression of the DQ brand and the longest-running dessert in American quick-service history.</p>
    <p>What makes DQ soft serve distinct from ordinary hard-scoop ice cream is both its proprietary formulation—fresh milk, cream, cane sugar, and whey—and its precise dispensing temperature. Poured at approximately 18°F (compared to hard ice cream frozen to 0°F or lower), Dairy Queen soft serve maintains an exceptionally velvety, pliable texture that coats the palate without numbing taste buds, allowing the fragrant vanilla flavor to shine.</p>

    <h2>2026 Prices, Sizing &amp; Calorie Breakdown</h2>
    <p>At an entry price of just <strong>$1.79 for a Small cone</strong>, the Vanilla Soft Serve Cone stands as the single highest-value and lowest-calorie sweet treat on the entire Dairy Queen menu:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Small ($1.79 · 170 cal · 5g Fat):</strong> The classic post-lunch refresher, curled to an iconic point on a crisp cake wafer cone.</li>
      <li><strong>Regular ($2.39 · 230 cal · 7g Fat):</strong> The standard size and universal fan favorite, delivering ample creamy swirls.</li>
      <li><strong>Large ($2.99 · 340 cal · 10g Fat):</strong> A towering soft-serve spire for true dairy purists.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cone Upgrades &amp; Classic Treat Comparisons</h2>
    <p>While the classic vanilla cone is delicious in its purest form, Dairy Queen offers several legendary dipped variations and dessert upgrades:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Treat Option</th><th>Price (Reg)</th><th>Calories</th><th>What Sets It Apart</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$2.39</td><td>230</td><td>The timeless baseline: pure vanilla soft serve on a wafer cone</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Chocolate Dipped Cone</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.19</td><td>330</td><td>Dipped in warm cocoa coating that forms a crunchy, crackling shell</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Crunchin' Cookie Dipped Cone</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>350</td><td>Chocolate shell loaded with crunchy cookie crumbs</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hot Fudge Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>300</td><td>Bowl presentation with warm, rich chocolate fudge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mini Oreo Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>~320</td><td>Spindle-blended with real Oreo cookie pieces</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>The Kids Meal &amp; Value Insider Tip</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Included in Every Kids Meal:</strong> Every $4.99 <a href="/categories/kids-meals">DQ Kids Meal</a> includes a complimentary Vanilla Soft Serve Cone (normally $1.79–$2.39 a la carte), making the children's combo an unbeatable family bargain.</li>
      <li><strong>Cup Option for Hot Days:</strong> If dining on a sweltering summer day or ordering for toddlers, ask the crew to dispense your cone upside-down into a cup ("cone in a cup") to catch every drip before it melts.</li>
      <li><strong>Dip Cone Customization:</strong> Most locations will gladly dip a Small or Large cone in chocolate upon request (~$0.80 upcharge).</li>
    </ul>

